O(1) Optimal solution+Intuition+Approach+TC&SC(965 Univalued Binary Tree)

Intuition
A binary tree is univalued if every node has the same value as the root.

Instead of using recursion or a queue/stack, we can traverse the tree while maintaining O(1) extra space using Morris Traversal.
This works by temporarily modifying the tree structure to simulate inorder traversal without recursion.

During traversal, we compare each visited node’s value with the root’s value. If any mismatch is found, the tree is not univalued.

Approach
Store the root’s value as reference (val = root->val).
Initialize curr = root.
While curr is not NULL:
If curr->left is NULL:
Check value of curr
Move to curr->right
Else:
Find inorder predecessor (ip) in left subtree
If ip->right is NULL:
Create thread (ip->right = curr)
Move left
Else:
Remove thread (ip->right = NULL)
Check curr->val
Move right
If all nodes match, return true.
Complexity
Time complexity:
O(n)
Each node is visited at most 2 times (thread creation and removal).

Space complexity:
O(1)
No recursion stack or auxiliary data structure is used.
Only a few pointers are used for traversal.

Code
/**
 * Definition for a binary tree node.
 * struct TreeNode {
 *     int val;
 *     TreeNode *left;
 *     TreeNode *right;
 *     TreeNode() : val(0), left(nullptr), right(nullptr) {}
 *     TreeNode(int x) : val(x), left(nullptr), right(nullptr) {}
 *     TreeNode(int x, TreeNode *left, TreeNode *right) : val(x), left(left), right(right) {}
 * };
 */
class Solution {
public:
    bool isUnivalTree(TreeNode* root) {
        if(root==nullptr){
            return true;
        }
        
        int val=root->val;
        TreeNode* curr=root;
        bool res=true;

        while(curr!=nullptr){
            if(curr->left==nullptr){
                if(curr->val!=val){
                    res=false;
                }
                curr=curr->right;
            }
            else{
                TreeNode* ip=curr->left;
                while(ip->right!=nullptr && ip->right!=curr){
                    ip=ip->right;
                }

                if(ip->right==nullptr){
                    ip->right=curr;
                    curr=curr->left;
                }
                else if(ip->right==curr){
                    ip->right=nullptr;
                    if(curr->val!=val){
                        res=false;
                    }
                    curr=curr->right;
                }
            }
        }

        return res;
    }
};
